{
  "model": "gemma4:12b",
  "created_at": "2026-07-01T21:59:00.5673606Z",
  "response": "{\"campaign_title\": \"The Echoes of the Drift\", \"campaign_subtitle\": \"A Long Way from Home.\", \"campaign_logline\": \"In a dying nebula and a fractured system, a broken pilot finds purpose in the trade routes between three warring factions and one mysterious broker.\", \"campaign_pitch\": \"You are not a hero. You are a scavenger of space. The 'Echoes of' title refers to findngs left behind by old tech. You start with a beat-up ship and a debt that can only be paid off in parts. Navigate the friction between Zenith (Technocracy), Aurelia (Trade Guild), and Vanguard (Militarist). Survive the grind, work for Kaelen, and see what lies beyond the gates.\", \"campaign_story_summary\": \"The system is dying. The trade routes are failing. Between the Zenith tech-elite who want to be perfect, the Zenith-Aurelia alliance of commerce, and the Vanguard's hardline military stance, a balance of power is destroyed. Kaelen acts as the neutral ground between these three. You work for her because she pays in real credits. The story focuses on your growth from a less-era than a mere courier to a respected contractor.\", \"tone\": \"Dry, gritty, slightly ironic frontier humor. Think 'Space Trucker' with a bit of feel.\", \"opening\": {\n    \"status_quo\": \"The system is in a state of decay. The 'Great Gate' connection is flickering and unstable. You are a pilot who lost their ship-title to a bank, and your current vessel, the 'Stubborn Mule', is barely holding together. You live for the next paycheck.\",\n    \"visible_crisis\": \"The trade routes between Zenith Prime and Aurelia Outpost are being contested by Vanguard patrols. The friction creates a 'gray zone' where contraband and salvaged scrap are high- valueed.\",\n    \"hidden_crisis\": \"The gate network is decaying biologically, and the few who know it is failing, are trying to cover up the fact that they are truly dying.\",\n    \"why_now\": \"A sudden surge in the turn of a 'ghost' signal from the core of the space-fold. It has triggered an emergency protocol in local sensors. This means your first paycheck will be more valuable than usual.\",\n    \"player_role\": \"You are a low-priority courier and scavenger. You start with no special destiny; you are just trying to make enough credits to keep your oxygen scrubber running.\"\n},\n\"mystery\": {\n    \"question\": \"What is the source of the turn? (Note: This must not be solved in this campaign.)\",\n    \"false_answer\": \"The signal is a remnant of an ancient civilization's communication. \",\n    \"true_answer_hint\": \"Something else is listening.\",\n    \"long_term_reveal_direction\": \"Future campaigns will find the truth, but for you, it is just static in the space-fold.\"\n},\n\"kaelen\": {\n    \"public_role\": \"Broker and Fixer. She handles contracts and logistics.\",\n    \"secret_angle\": \"She knows exactly why the gate network is failing, but she chooses to stay out of politics and just wants a local fact.\",\n    \"address_rule\": \"Kaelen never speaks about her past or her work with the core-gate mechanics. She only talks business.\",\n    \"never_reveal_rule\": \"She will always be available as your primary contact for contracts.\"\n},\n  \"factions\": {\n    \"zenith_problem\": \"The Zenith elite are obsessed with perfection and automation. They want to automate the core-surance. You struggle to find a way to balance their need for tech and the people who are player-aware.\",\n    \"aurelia_problem\": \"Aurelia is all about the profit margin. They don't care what they, mean as long as you deliver the package. If it breaks, it's your problem.\",\n    \"vanguard_problem\": \"The Vanguard are hardline and uncompromising. They can only see the world in terms of segments and targets. They want to order on the space-fold.\",\n    \"conflict_triangle\": \"You move between these three as a neutral party, and their demands often conflict.\",\n    \"neutral_space_pressure\": \"The trade routes are becoming more dangerous because of the 'gray zone' where the other factions' jurisdictions overlap. You'll have to choose who to support during cargo delivery.\"\n  },\n  \"act_1\": {\n    \"name\": \"The Broken Link\",\n    \"goal\": \"Establish a sense of scale and basic mechanics.\",\n    \"opening_incident\": \"You are contracted by Kaelen to haul a 'stable' shipment of minerals from an Aurelia mining outpost. During the transport, you encounter a pirate ship (a Reaver) which attacks your cargo-ship. You must survive and defend yourself against this one hostile.\",\n    \"midpoint_turn\": \"After winning, the fight is revealed to be part of a test for Kaelen's 'Specialized Contracts'. You are now officially on her list.\",\n    \"finale\": \"You deliver the shipment to Zenith Prime. Upon delivery, you have a100% trust-score with some Aurelia allies and a certain amount of credits.\",\n    \"player_takeaway\": \"The universe is large, but you're just trying to see the one next of day.\"\n  },\n  \"starter_mission\": {\n    \"title\": \"First Blood\",\n    \"reason\": \"This mission provides a tutorial on combat and defense.\",\n    \"enemy_identity\": \"A single Reaver-class vessel, 'The Scraps', a pirate ship with a haven't even a name of sense. They are just trying to take your cargo.\",\n    \"enemy_knows\": \"They don't know you are not important; they are only interested in your haul.\",\n    \"aftershock\": \"You get paid and a ship-title for 'The Scrappard'. The first mention of the 'ghost signal' is heard over public radio.\"\n  },\n  \"recurring_clue\":\n  {\n    \"name\": \"The Drift\",\n    \"signal\": \"A recurring, low-frequency pulse from the station-core. It sounds like a dying heartbeat.\",\n    \"first_appearance\": \"You hear it during your first combat mission.\",\n    \"escalation\": \"Other pilots are system-wide; some say they's just static, but Kaelen seems to listen and wait.\",\n    \"payoff_hint\": \"It is a signal that will be sent in another campaign. It won't be solved here.\"\n  },\n  \"rumor_trail\": {\n",
